<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/17th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battles of Guararapes</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1648">1648</a>–<a href="/years/1649">1649</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-portuguese-war">Dutch–Portuguese War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battles of Guararapes were two battles fought in April 1648 and February 1649 on the Guararapes hills south of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/recife">Recife</a> in north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a>. Portuguese, Brazilian, Indigenous and African forces of the Pernambuco insurrection defeated the army of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-west-india-company">Dutch West India Company</a> both times. The defeats confined the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> to Recife, which surrendered in 1654, and the first battle is regarded as the origin of the Brazilian Army.</p></div>
